# SAMPLE ONLY - not a real certificate.
#
# Feed server TLS certificate, used when FEED_DISTRIBUTOR_HTTPS_ENABLED=true.
#
# What to do:
#   1. Put your certificate in this folder as "server.crt" (no ".sample").
#      The folder is mounted read-only at /certs, so the default setting
#      FEED_DISTRIBUTOR_TLS_CERT_FILE=/certs/server.crt finds it.
#   2. Make it readable by UID 10001 (the container user).
#   3. Delete this sample file if you like; it is never read.
#
# Format: PEM text (Base64 between BEGIN/END CERTIFICATE lines), as the full
# chain in this order:
#   - the server certificate (its subject or SAN matches the hostname
#     the clients use in the feed URL)
#   - then each intermediate CA certificate
#   - the root CA is optional
#
# Use a certificate from an internal or public CA: most clients validate it
# and reject a self-signed one unless its CA is imported.
#
# Check the file:  openssl x509 -in server.crt -noout -subject -issuer -enddate
